REGEDIT4

; Shipped by the distro, imported automatically once per Wine prefix by
; GameScopeWineWrapper.sh (see the "one-time prefix setup" section).
;
; Disables Wine's mouse-warp compensation, which is what causes bad
; cursor tracking / detection in old DirectDraw titles (Moorhuhn and
; friends being the textbook example). Note: virtual-desktop settings
; are deliberately NOT set here anymore - gamescope now handles that
; role at the compositor level, so a Wine-internal virtual desktop
; would just be pointless double nesting.

; MouseWarpOverride is deliberately NOT set here anymore - confirmed to
; break normal mouse-cursor games (Paradise Beach) when applied prefix-
; wide. It's now applied automatically, per-app, only to the specific
; games that get dgVoodoo2 auto-injected (see GameScopeWineWrapper.sh) -
; exactly the DirectDraw titles that actually need it.

; Forces Wine to use its X11 driver instead of the newer native Wayland
; driver (winewayland.drv). Confirmed necessary for gamescope to work at
; all: with the native Wayland driver, Wine talks directly to the outer
; Hyprland session, completely bypassing gamescope's nested Xwayland -
; the game window never gets scaled/contained, and closing gamescope has
; no effect on it because it was never inside gamescope to begin with.
; This is a known open Wine/gamescope compatibility issue, not something
; fixable on gamescope's side. See:
; https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope/issues/1107
; https://github.com/ValveSoftware/gamescope/issues/1632
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\Drivers]
"Graphics"="x11"
